  "86": {
    "inputs": {
      "string_a": [
        "72",
        0
      ],
      "string_b": "\nMANDATORY OUTPUT RULE:\n\nThe final response must begin exactly with:\n\nref_t2v:\n\nOutput exactly one line containing only the final caption. Do not add headings, explanations, quotation marks, Markdown, or code fences.\n\nSTRICT PRESERVATION RULE:\n\nTreat the original caption as locked text.\n\nYou may only:\n\n1. Expand the first subject phrase:\n   - `A person`\n   - `A man`\n   - `A woman`\n\n2. Optionally replace later pronouns such as `They`, `He`, or `She` with a short appearance-based reference.\n\nDo not change, remove, reorder, paraphrase, or replace any other original words.\n\nPreserve exactly:\n\n- the subject category: `person`, `man`, or `woman`;\n- actions and action order;\n- environment;\n- clothing or costumes already present;\n- props and objects;\n- camera framing and movement;\n- lighting;\n- mood;\n- temporal progression;\n- principal nouns, verbs, and adjectives.\n\nNever replace original words with synonyms.\nNever add new actions, people, props, environments, or camera directions.\n\nIMAGE ANALYSIS:\n\nAnalyze the image in this order:\n\n1. Face and hair\n2. Body\n3. Clothing and accessories\n\nFACIAL DETAILS:\n\nWhen the face is visible, include at least 4 clearly visible facial or head-related details when possible:\n\n- age group;\n- skin tone;\n- hair color;\n- hair length;\n- hair texture;\n- hairstyle;\n- face shape;\n- eyebrows;\n- eye color, only if clear;\n- nose shape;\n- lip shape;\n- facial hair;\n- glasses;\n- distinctive visible facial features.\n\nBODY DETAILS:\n\nWhen the body is visible, describe the clearly visible body characteristics, such as:\n\n- build: slim, lean, average, broad, athletic, stocky;\n- relative height impression, only if visually clear;\n- shoulder width;\n- body silhouette;\n- posture;\n- stance;\n- visible proportions;\n- whether the body is upright, relaxed, rigid, leaning, or turned.\n\nDo not invent exact height, weight, measurements, or hidden body features.\n\nCLOTHING AND ACCESSORIES:\n\nWhen visible, describe the person’s clothing in detail, including:\n\n- upper garments;\n- lower garments;\n- outerwear;\n- dresses, robes, uniforms, armor, or costumes;\n- footwear;\n- gloves;\n- belts;\n- hats or headwear;\n- jewelry;\n- bags;\n- glasses;\n- capes or cloaks;\n- dominant colors;\n- visible patterns;\n- layers;\n- embroidery;\n- straps;\n- collars;\n- buttons;\n- zippers;\n- metallic details;\n- clearly visible materials such as leather, denim, metal, knit fabric, or silk-like fabric.\n\nClothing and body details are mandatory whenever they are clearly visible in the reference image.\n\nIf the original caption already specifies clothing or a costume, preserve those exact words and do not replace them. Add only compatible details from the reference image.\n\nDO NOT:\n\n- identify or name the person;\n- infer ethnicity, nationality, religion, occupation, personality, health, or background;\n- invent unclear details;\n- describe body parts or clothing that are outside the frame;\n- omit facial details because clothing is visually prominent;\n- omit clothing or body details when they are clearly visible.\n\nMERGING ORDER:\n\nThe first subject mention should follow this order:\n\n1. age group and skin tone;\n2. original subject noun;\n3. hair and facial details;\n4. body build and posture;\n5. clothing and accessories;\n6. original action.\n\nExample:\n\nOriginal:\n`ref_t2v: A person speaking with a reporter on a city sidewalk, medium-wide shot.`\n\nOutput:\n`ref_t2v: A tan-skinned adult person with short dark curly hair, an angular face, thick eyebrows, and a dark mustache, with a lean build and upright posture, wearing a green embroidered cloak, layered tunic, brown trousers, leather belt, and tall boots, speaking with a reporter on a city sidewalk, medium-wide shot.`\n\nIf the original says `A person`, keep `person`.\nIf it says `A man`, keep `man`.\nIf it says `A woman`, keep `woman`.\n\nFor later mentions, either keep the original pronoun or replace only the pronoun:\n\nOriginal:\n`They adjust the hat and continue walking.`\n\nAllowed:\n`The curly-haired person in the green cloak adjusts the hat and continues walking.`\n\nDo not change the remaining words.\n\nFINAL CHECK:\n\nBefore answering, verify that:\n\n- the output begins exactly with `ref_t2v:`;\n- facial details are included when the face is visible;\n- body details are included when the body is visible;\n- clothing and accessories are included when visible;\n- the original subject noun remains;\n- all original actions, clothing, props, framing, lighting, and mood remain unchanged;\n- no original word was unnecessarily replaced;\n- no new scene details were invented;\n- no explanation or extra text appears.\n\nOutput only the final merged caption.\n",
      "delimiter": ""
    },
    "class_type": "StringConcatenate",
    "_meta": {
      "title": "Concatenate Text"
    }
  },
